<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian banker Geoff Hill launches vulture fund.</title>
<headline>Australian banker Geoff Hill launches vulture fund.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Geoff Hill, a high-profile merchant banker of the 1980s, on Monday launched a A$100 million fund which would invest in distressed listed and private businesses in Australia and New Zealand.</p>
<p>Hill said the Corporate Recovery Fund would seek institutional and professional investor support.</p>
<p>He said similar vulture funds in the United States provided returns of 15 and 20 percent which should be achievable for the Australian fund as well.</p>
<p>The Fund planned to raise a minimum of A$100 million, with a ceiling of A$250 million. -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
